nt.get` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts in total, waiting 0.5 s and then 1 s between them (the delay doubles each time). The change is in `weather.py`.\n\n- **Only 503 is retried.** Any other HTTP error, and any network or timeout error, is raised right away.\n- **After the third 503**, the last `HTTPError` is raised to the caller.\n- **The 503 response is closed before each retry**, so connections aren't left open.\n- **Settings:** the attempt count and starting delay are class attributes (`max_attempts = 3`, `backoff_base = 0.5`). You can change them per client or in tests.\n\nI tested it against a real local HTTP server, with the delay shortened to 0.05 s:\n\n| Server behaviour | Result | Requests |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, then 200 | returns the JSON | 3 |\n| 503 three times | raises `HTTPError 503` | 3 |\n| 500 | raises `HTTPError 500` with no retry | 1 |\n\nI didn't add a test file, because the repo has no test suite.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 70129, "requests_cache_write": 108138, "requests_cost_usd": 0.5892238, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1723, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 61, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:38:11.374714+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 36.539, "t_checker_s": 2.58, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1735, "t